   1: """D3 + C6: Schema.org JSON-LD + lightweight accessibility patches.
   2: 
   3: D3. For every *.html page, inject a Schema.org `MedicalScholarlyArticle`
   4:     JSON-LD block in <head>:
   5:       - headline      = page <title>
   6:       - description   = existing meta description (D1) or PICO digest
   7:       - datePublished = file mtime (best-available signal)
   8:       - dateModified  = same
   9:       - author        = Mahmood Ahmad
  10:       - publisher     = RapidMeta (Organization)
  11:       - url           = canonical https://...github.io/.../<file>
  12:       - about         = first PICO `cond` or `condition`
  13:       - keywords      = drug + condition + 'meta-analysis, living review'
  14:     Skip if a JSON-LD block already exists.
  15: 
  16: C6. Three low-risk a11y improvements:
  17:       - Ensure <html lang="en"> is set (some pages don't have it).
  18:       - Inject a "skip to main content" link as the first <body> child for
  19:         keyboard users (visually hidden, focus-visible).
  20:       - Add aria-label to icon-only <button>/<a> elements that have no
  21:         text content but do have an onclick/href. Uses the `title=` attr
  22:         when present, else falls back to the icon class name or a sensible
  23:         default ("Action button").
  24: 
  25: Both passes are idempotent â€” they each leave a marker comment so re-runs
  26: detect previous injections and no-op.
  27: """
  28: from __future__ import annotations
  29: import json
  30: import re
  31: import sys
  32: import io
  33: from datetime import date
  34: from pathlib import Path
  35: 
  36: if "pytest" not in sys.modules and hasattr(sys.stdout, "buffer"):
  37:     sys.stdout = io.TextIOWrapper(sys.stdout.buffer, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
  38: 
  39: HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
  40: PAGES_BASE = "https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/rapidmeta-finerenone/"
  41: 
  42: TITLE_RE = re.compile(r"<title>(.*?)</title>", re.DOTALL | re.IGNORECASE)
  43: DESC_RE = re.compile(r'<meta\s+name="description"\s+content="([^"]*)"', re.IGNORECASE)
  44: HEAD_END_RE = re.compile(r"</head>", re.IGNORECASE)
  45: PICO_FIELD_RE = re.compile(r"\b(pop|int|comp|out|drug|cond|condition):\s*'((?:[^'\\]|\\.)*)'")
  46: HTML_OPEN_RE = re.compile(r"<html(\s[^>]*)?>", re.IGNORECASE)
  47: BODY_OPEN_RE = re.compile(r"<body(\s[^>]*)?>", re.IGNORECASE)
  48: 
  49: JSONLD_MARK = "<!-- jsonld:begin -->"
  50: JSONLD_END = "<!-- jsonld:end -->"
  51: SKIPLINK_MARK = "<!-- a11y-skiplink:begin -->"
  52: SKIPLINK_END = "<!-- a11y-skiplink:end -->"
  53: 
  54: SKIPLINK_BLOCK = (
  55:     f"{SKIPLINK_MARK}\n"
  56:     '<a href="#main" class="rm-a11y-skiplink" '
  57:     'style="position:absolute;left:-999px;top:auto;width:1px;height:1px;'
  58:     'overflow:hidden;z-index:9999;background:#0b1220;color:#fff;'
  59:     'padding:8px 12px;border-radius:0 0 6px 0;text-decoration:none;'
  60:     'font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;font-size:14px;" '
  61:     'onfocus="this.style.left=\'0\';this.style.top=\'0\';this.style.width=\'auto\';'
  62:     'this.style.height=\'auto\';" '
  63:     'onblur="this.style.left=\'-999px\';">Skip to main content</a>\n'
  64:     f"{SKIPLINK_END}"
  65: )
  66: 
  67: 
  68: def extract_first_pico(txt: str, key: str) -> str | None:
  69:     for m in PICO_FIELD_RE.finditer(txt):
  70:         if m.group(1) == key:
  71:             return m.group(2).replace("\\'", "'")
  72:     return None
  73: 
  74: 
  75: def jsonld_for(p: Path, txt: str) -> str | None:
  76:     if JSONLD_MARK in txt:
  77:         return None  # already injected
  78:     title_m = TITLE_RE.search(txt)
  79:     headline = title_m.group(1).strip() if title_m else p.stem.replace("_", " ").title()
  80:     desc_m = DESC_RE.search(txt)
  81:     description = desc_m.group(1).strip() if desc_m else None
  82: 
  83:     drug = extract_first_pico(txt, "drug") or extract_first_pico(txt, "int")
  84:     cond = extract_first_pico(txt, "cond") or extract_first_pico(txt, "condition")
  85:     if drug:
  86:         drug = drug.split("(")[0].strip()
  87:     if cond:
  88:         cond = cond.split("(")[0].strip()
  89:     keywords = ["meta-analysis", "living review", "RapidMeta"]
  90:     if drug:
  91:         keywords.append(drug)
  92:     if cond:
  93:         keywords.append(cond)
  94: 
  95:     mtime = date.fromtimestamp(p.stat().st_mtime).isoformat()
  96:     url = PAGES_BASE if p.name == "index.html" else PAGES_BASE + p.name
  97: 
  98:     payload = {
  99:         "@context": "https://schema.org",
 100:         "@type": "MedicalScholarlyArticle",
 101:         "headline": _clean(headline),
 102:         "name": _clean(headline),
 103:         "url": url,
 104:         "datePublished": mtime,
 105:         "dateModified": mtime,
 106:         "inLanguage": "en",
 107:         "author": {
 108:             "@type": "Person",
 109:             "name": "Mahmood Ahmad",
 110:             "identifier": "https://orcid.org/",
 111:         },
 112:         "publisher": {
 113:             "@type": "Organization",
 114:             "name": "RapidMeta",
 115:             "url": PAGES_BASE,
 116:         },
 117:         "isAccessibleForFree": True,
 118:         "keywords": ", ".join(keywords),
 119:     }
 120:     if description:
 121:         payload["description"] = description[:5000]
 122:     if cond:
 123:         payload["about"] = {"@type": "MedicalCondition", "name": cond}
 124:     if drug:
 125:         payload["mentions"] = {"@type": "Drug", "name": drug}
 126: 
 127:     json_str = json.dumps(payload, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False)
 128:     return (
 129:         f"{JSONLD_MARK}\n"
 130:         f'<script type="application/ld+json">{json_str}</script>\n'
 131:         f"{JSONLD_END}"
 132:     )
 133: 
 134: 
 135: def _clean(s: str) -> str:
 136:     s = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", s).strip()
 137:     return s[:300]
 138: 
 139: 
 140: def patch_html(p: Path) -> dict:
 141:     txt = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
 142:     orig = txt
 143:     stats = {"jsonld": False, "lang": False, "skiplink": False, "aria": 0}
 144: 
 145:     # D3 JSON-LD
 146:     block = jsonld_for(p, txt)
 147:     if block and "</head>" in txt:
 148:         txt = txt.replace("</head>", block + "\n</head>", 1)
 149:         stats["jsonld"] = True
 150: 
 151:     # C6.1 <html lang="en">
 152:     html_m = HTML_OPEN_RE.search(txt)
 153:     if html_m and "lang=" not in html_m.group(0):
 154:         new_open = html_m.group(0).replace("<html", '<html lang="en"', 1)
 155:         txt = txt[: html_m.start()] + new_open + txt[html_m.end():]
 156:         stats["lang"] = True
 157: 
 158:     # C6.2 skip-link
 159:     if SKIPLINK_MARK not in txt and "<body" in txt:
 160:         # Insert right after the opening <body ...>
 161:         body_m = BODY_OPEN_RE.search(txt)
 162:         if body_m:
 163:             insert_at = body_m.end()
 164:             txt = txt[:insert_at] + "\n" + SKIPLINK_BLOCK + txt[insert_at:]
 165:             stats["skiplink"] = True
 166:             # Add id="main" to the first content container if it doesn't already have one.
 167:             main_m = re.search(r'<main(\s[^>]*)?>', txt[insert_at + len(SKIPLINK_BLOCK):], re.IGNORECASE)
 168:             if main_m:
 169:                 seg_start = insert_at + len(SKIPLINK_BLOCK)
 170:                 mm = re.search(r'<main(\s[^>]*)?>', txt[seg_start:], re.IGNORECASE)
 171:                 attrs = mm.group(1) or ""
 172:                 if 'id=' not in attrs:
 173:                     repl = f'<main id="main"{attrs}>'
 174:                     txt = txt[: seg_start + mm.start()] + repl + txt[seg_start + mm.end():]
 175: 
 176:     # C6.3 aria-label on empty button/anchor with onclick/href but no text
 177:     # Only target buttons/anchors that contain a single <i class="..."> icon and no text node.
 178:     def add_aria(match):
 179:         tag = match.group(0)
 180:         if "aria-label" in tag:
 181:             return tag
 182:         title_m = re.search(r'\btitle="([^"]+)"', tag)
 183:         label = title_m.group(1) if title_m else None
 184:         if not label:
 185:             # Try data-tooltip / data-action.
 186:             for attr in ("data-tooltip", "data-action", "aria-labelledby"):
 187:                 m2 = re.search(rf'\b{attr}="([^"]+)"', tag)
 188:                 if m2:
 189:                     label = m2.group(1); break
 190:         if not label:
 191:             label = "Toolbar action"
 192:         stats["aria"] += 1
 193:         # Insert aria-label right after the tag name.
 194:         return re.sub(r"^<(\w+)", rf'<\1 aria-label="{label}"', tag, count=1)
 195: 
 196:     txt = re.sub(
 197:         r'<button(?![^>]*aria-label)[^>]*>\s*<i\s+class="[^"]*"\s*></i>\s*</button>',
 198:         add_aria, txt,
 199:     )
 200: 
 201:     if txt != orig:
 202:         p.write_text(txt, encoding="utf-8")
 203:     return stats
 204: 
 205: 
 206: def main():
 207:     targets = sorted(p for p in HERE.glob("*.html") if p.is_file())
 208:     print(f"Scanning {len(targets):,} pages...")
 209:     n_jsonld = n_lang = n_skip = n_aria = 0
 210:     files_touched = 0
 211:     for i, p in enumerate(targets, 1):
 212:         s = patch_html(p)
 213:         if any([s["jsonld"], s["lang"], s["skiplink"], s["aria"]]):
 214:             files_touched += 1
 215:         n_jsonld += int(s["jsonld"])
 216:         n_lang += int(s["lang"])
 217:         n_skip += int(s["skiplink"])
 218:         n_aria += s["aria"]
 219:         if i % 300 == 0:
 220:             print(f"  [{i}/{len(targets)}] {p.name}")
 221:     print(f"\nFiles touched          : {files_touched:,}")
 222:     print(f"  JSON-LD injected     : {n_jsonld:,}")
 223:     print(f"  <html lang> added    : {n_lang:,}")
 224:     print(f"  skip-link added      : {n_skip:,}")
 225:     print(f"  aria-label added     : {n_aria:,} buttons")
 226: 
 227: 
 228: if __name__ == "__main__":
 229:     main()

codex
Defects found:

- `idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment/marker` — line 76.  
  Input: `<html><head><title>T</title></head><body><!-- jsonld:begin --></body></html>`  
  Consequence: JSON-LD is skipped even though no JSON-LD block exists.

- `idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment/marker` — line 76.  
  Input: `<html><head><title>T</title><script type="application/ld+json">{}</script></head><body></body></html>`  
  Consequence: an existing unmarked JSON-LD block is not detected, so a duplicate block is injected.

- `idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment/marker` — line 159.  
  Input: `<html><body><!-- a11y-skiplink:begin --><main></main></body></html>`  
  Consequence: the skip link is skipped because the marker exists, not because the skip link exists.

- `selector keyed to a form the corpus may not use` — lines 147-148.  
  Input: `<html><HEAD><title>T</title></HEAD><body></body></html>`  
  Consequence: JSON-LD is not injected because the code defines a case-insensitive `HEAD_END_RE` but uses literal lowercase `"</head>"`.

- `selector keyed to a form the corpus may not use` — line 159.  
  Input: `<html><head></head><BODY><main></main></BODY></html>`  
  Consequence: the skip link is not injected because the precheck looks for literal lowercase `"<body"` before using the case-insensitive regex.

- `idempotency/selector guard satisfied by the wrong attribute` — line 153.  
  Input: `<html data-lang="fr"><head></head><body></body></html>`  
  Consequence: `<html lang="en">` is not added because `data-lang=` satisfies the substring test.

- `idempotency/selector guard satisfied by the wrong attribute` — line 172.  
  Input: `<html><body><main data-id="x"></main></body></html>`  
  Consequence: `id="main"` is not added, so the injected skip link points to a missing target.

- `selector keyed to a form the stated target includes but the regex excludes` — lines 176-198.  
  Input: `<a href="/next"><i class="fa fa-arrow-right"></i></a>`  
  Consequence: icon-only anchors never receive `aria-label`, despite the comment saying buttons/anchors are targeted.

No proven CRLF/LF text-comparison defect.  
No proven merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation defect.  
No proven zero-conflated-with-absent defect.  
No proven negation-dropped defect.  
No proven different-copy instrumentation defect from this file alone.
